  "retired_e2e_cases": [
    {
      "case": "qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-chunked-prefill",
      "source_path": "crates/core/parity_tests/perfmodel/goldens/afd_e2e.json",
      "attribution": "Chunked prefill: engine.afd.chunked_prefill_size=256 < isl=1024 splits each prompt into 4 chunks on SGLang's native chunked-prefill path. Each prefill pass is priced by the aic-afd provider at its actual (chunk tokens, prefix) geometry (attention grows with the real prefix, F-pool cost tracks chunk tokens) — never a full frozen prompt step. The caliber change is physical, not an error: TTFT pays one full pipeline step per chunk (fill included, conservative per-pass fill — see the fill-amortized case), and decode interleaves with chunk passes (mean_tpot_ms roughly doubles vs the pinned single-pass case). Default behavior is unchanged: without an explicit chunked_prefill_size the window stays pinned at the prompt length.",
      "source_record_sha256": "2e6b6ebf0164bbd4ecd4fe2b88e64b9b3aa578e5217691c5b39f385f5b432dc2"
    },
    {
      "case": "qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-pd-decode",
      "source_path": "crates/core/parity_tests/perfmodel/goldens/afd_e2e.json",
      "attribution": "afd+pd on the continuous SGLang core: the AFD pool serves one phase as a disagg role (aic-afd provider injected via PerfModel::External) paired with a monolithic companion on the generic DestinationFirst handoff surface (backend sglang 0.5.14, h200_sxm). Caliber note: the generic destination convention produces ALL osl tokens at the destination (the source-side first-token signal marks TTFT/conformance only and is not counted in report totals), so an AFD decode role runs one more decode pass per request than the retired Python island's osl-1 convention; TTFT includes the first destination decode pass. Per-worker GPU accounting reports the A/F pool-pair total (16) on the AFD role and tp (8) on the companion. Same data caveat as the pure case: h200_sxm sglang lacks mla_bmm rows (trtllm 1.3.0rc20 fallback, warned at load).",
      "source_record_sha256": "62d4770bed38a3212660f49936dd64fd089c31bccbbf37a3a5c1a4999c188ebe"
    },
    {
      "case": "qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-pd-prefill",
      "source_path": "crates/core/parity_tests/perfmodel/goldens/afd_e2e.json",
      "attribution": "afd+pd on the continuous SGLang core: the AFD pool serves one phase as a disagg role (aic-afd provider injected via PerfModel::External) paired with a monolithic companion on the generic DestinationFirst handoff surface (backend sglang 0.5.14, h200_sxm). Caliber note: the generic destination convention produces ALL osl tokens at the destination (the source-side first-token signal marks TTFT/conformance only and is not counted in report totals), so an AFD decode role runs one more decode pass per request than the retired Python island's osl-1 convention; TTFT includes the first destination decode pass. Per-worker GPU accounting reports the A/F pool-pair total (16) on the AFD role and tp (8) on the companion. Same data caveat as the pure case: h200_sxm sglang lacks mla_bmm rows (trtllm 1.3.0rc20 fallback, warned at load).",
      "source_record_sha256": "293573a1b427fd98f7880eb4847fd1d66b1b3637d08a6c139f3d7ba4f08db986"
    },
    {
      "case": "qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-pure-both",
      "source_path": "crates/core/parity_tests/perfmodel/goldens/afd_e2e.json",
      "attribution": "Continuous-batching rebuild: the AFD pool now runs on the SGLang continuous scheduler (mid-flight admission + retraction) with the aic-afd timing provider injected, anchoring the sglang perf-DB family (0.5.14); the retired batch-locked AfdCore + trtllm anchor is not comparable and was dropped (mean_ttft_ms 422.1866311464918 / mean_tpot_ms 11.846695674852583 at a_batch_size=18). The afd+pd cases (pd-decode / pd-prefill) run on the same continuous core with a monolithic companion. One data caveat: the h200_sxm sglang family lacks mla_bmm rows, so that op family falls back to trtllm 1.3.0rc20 data (framework-implicit, warned at load).",
      "source_record_sha256": "f45cbcef3a0c71050a5784935736c318e352a13b47846a264e1fc2f575964c3d"
    },
    {
      "case": "qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-pure-both-saturated",
      "source_path": "crates/core/parity_tests/perfmodel/goldens/afd_e2e.json",
      "attribution": "Saturated admission anchor: identical topology, backend_version and perf-DB family to qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-pure-both, with concurrency 24 pushed above the pool's in-flight cap (max_num_seqs = n_a_workers 1 * a_batch_size 18 = 18) and 64 total requests, so every pass has work queued. Pins the saturated side of the admission boundary that the unsaturated case cannot reach: the radix memory reserve must not bind below max_num_seqs, each 1024-token prompt must pre-fill in a single pass at the derived prompt window (the AFD timing identity charges one frozen prefill step per pass), and no retraction may fire across the whole run. Companion scheduler-level evidence: continuous_afd_derivation_keeps_max_num_seqs_as_the_only_binding_limit in crates/core/src/engine/scheduler/sglang/tests.rs. Not an anchor for the microbatch geometry clamp: a_batch_size 18 / num_microbatches 3 divides evenly, so the saturated short-circuit and the legacy clamp path price this workload identically.",
      "source_record_sha256": "fc88440e0d6f59b1d3b2da912145b787207a75b1f0ba066f01b69c9e3a85c879"
    },
    {
      "case": "qwen3-32b-h200-sglang-two-stage",
      "source_path": "crates/core/parity_tests/perfmodel/goldens/afd_e2e.json",
      "attribution": "Two shared resources execute A + A_to_F and F + F_to_A continuously per microbatch. Every pass includes startup, waiting and drain time. This case replaces the retired fill-amortized fixture; its original description is retained as historical attribution.",
      "source_record_sha256": "5b5560dfbe62cb03deac8db03bb8f2a28dcc48a8326a4bb54ecd15d6c0786b7f"
    }
  ],
